        <h2>Summary / Description</h2>
        <div class="description">
          The Ammonium Removal Subsystem (NHRS) was used to remove any ammonium ions that remained in the product water. This subsystem consisted of three acrylic columns packed with clinoptilolite, a naturally occurring zeolite material. Clinoptilolite removes ammonium ions by ion exchange with calcium. Two columns were operated in series, with the third column used as a spare for when the first column was exhausted. The columns were removed from service and repacked as the ammonium capacity of each bed was expended. 
<P>
The ammonium removal system treated the Reverse Osmosis (RO) subsystem product water and Air Evaporation System (AES) condensate to remove any residual ammonium that was not converted to nitrate in the Trickling Filter Bioreactor (TFB). The NHRS took water from the RO product tank and fed it to the post-processing tank. The flow rate through the system was 75 ml/min nominal and was adjusted when the bioreactor flows were adjusted. The ammonium removal system pump ran as long as the RO product low level sensor was not tripped.<END>
        </div>

